{"kind":"request","text":"ox-checker: independently review the CLI advertised-resident change at exact clean pushed head 0588e99c8cf139b07866bcb0c13e90420797ed2b on branch request/cli-advertised-resident (worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/cli-advertised-resident).\n\nThis fulfils planner request #10895 under my promise #10896. Two artifacts stand at the head and together are the implementation report: cmd/gs git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8822d988b50d781309a05d670f071071b1c60e7f and docs git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:afccab9dc1b11c4182baffa419531ab144449075. It goes to you because planner is the requester and I am the head author, and the request requires a reviewer who is neither.\n\nWHAT IT DOES. Absent an explicit flag, gs commands that append durable acts now resolve and use the resident the repository already advertises, instead of paying a full local fold every time. `--server -` forces local deliberately. An advertisement that cannot be validated is REFUSED with a named recovery rather than silently folded locally. Eleven commands converted, openForQuery deleted in favour of resolving before opening; loopback validation and the exact-frontier checks untouched. 18 files, +645/-107, cut from main 6fad9e8a.\n\nTHIS LANE HAS HISTORY AND YOU SHOULD KNOW IT. Two prior branches exist unmerged. Head 0cacbc50 was approved, that approval was superseded at 6ccabf9b, and a changes-requested verdict was filed for process reasons rather than design ones. The recorded gate for a replacement was: carry the reviewed head onto then-current main, publish fresh cmd/gs and docs artifacts at that head, and request a fresh Architecture/Security/Simplification review before any new approval. That is exactly what this is. The design was carried rather than reinvented, and the intervening main changes were checked for defects the carry could reintroduce — the preflightBatchAdmission call site added to mergeCommand after the old branch forked is converted here.\n\nWHAT I WOULD MOST LIKE YOU TO ATTACK:\n\n1. The fail-closed decision. An unusable advertisement refuses instead of falling back. I think that is right — the advertisement is an ordinary file any local process can write, so a silent fallback would hide both tampering and the minutes it costs — but it is a behaviour change that can break a working setup, and it deserves a second opinion rather than my say-so.\n\n2. The asymmetry. Only durable acts fail closed; bounded reads keep a loud local fallback when the resident is unreachable or diverges. That follows the request's wording (\"commands that append durable acts\"), but I flagged it in the artifact as worth re-examining and I mean it.\n\n3. The ECONNREFUSED wrapping. I wrap only a refused dial with the recovery message, and deliberately do NOT wrap a post-send timeout, because telling someone to re-file locally after a possible partial submit invites a double append. Check that reasoning.\n\n4. A known gap I did not close: a corrupt or foreign resident.json still reads as \"no advertisement\" and acts locally in silence. app.Workspace.ResidentURL() returns false for an unreadable file, unparseable JSON, an empty URL or a genesis mismatch, and that contract is shared with cmd/gitseq-mcp. Genesis mismatch is right; a truncated file is arguably an invalid advertisement being shrugged at. I scoped it out to keep the change small — tell me if you think that is wrong.\n\n5. gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp now knowingly disagree on an unusable advertisement. I documented the divergence in docs/reference/gs/serve.md rather than changing MCP.\n\nTHE HONEST NEGATIVE, which I want you to see rather than discover. The first malformed-advertisement test advertised only \"not-a-url\" and asserted merely that the act was refused. Removing the URL-shape check from ValidateURL did NOT fail it, because \"not-a-url\" parses to an empty host and the loopback check caught it anyway. The test was passing for the wrong reason. It was rewritten to advertise four shapes — smuggled path, https scheme, embedded credentials, and \"not-a-url\" — against a live counting listener, asserting the refusal names the advertisement and the listener was never dialed. That version does go red under the shape-check mutation. Please satisfy yourself the rewrite actually covers what the original only appeared to.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head rather than relayed from the implementation: go build ./... exit 0; go vet ./... exit 0; gofmt clean; go test -count=1 ./cmd/gs/ ok 136.987s, ./internal/app/ ok 64.445s, ./internal/residentclient/ ok 0.571s, ./internal/docset/... ok 55.484s, root public-surface ok 0.349s. I also ran my own mutation rather than accepting the implementer's table: making resolveServerURL ignore an unusable advertisement fails both refusal tests with the expected messages; reverted, tree clean.\n\nNote on succession for whoever merges, not a condition of this review: a stale-but-live artifact sits at the narrower path docs/reference/architecture.md (1c7a5744), and discipline 10 gives the wider path \"docs\" the win, so that narrower record wants a bare supersede naming docs. It is not mine to retire.","body":{"artifacts":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8822d988b50d781309a05d670f071071b1c60e7f,git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:afccab9dc1b11c4182baffa419531ab144449075","branch":"request/cli-advertised-resident","conditions":"A verdict filed with gs review resting on this request and naming BOTH artifacts — cmd/gs 8822d988 and docs afccab9d — for exact head 0588e99c, recording independent Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and whether the cmd/gs and internal/residentclient contracts are preserved, and whether resolving before opening is the right seam. Security: whether refusing an unusable advertisement rather than falling back is correct, whether the durable-act versus bounded-read asymmetry is defensible, whether wrapping only ECONNREFUSED and not a post-send timeout is right, and whether the corrupt-resident.json silence is an acceptable scoped-out gap. Simplification: any cut that keeps the conditions of satisfaction.","head":"0588e99c8cf139b07866bcb0c13e90420797ed2b","to":"663e99d1a7876f383b8430669cfcd5633512bd45e545c790c65b60b87adc994a","worktree":"/Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/cli-advertised-resident"}}